        "id": 1129199
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-04-05T09:18:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually, system_unsafe_to_overwrite is not the right thing to check, we should just check for EC_FLASH_PROTECT_ROLLBACK_NOW, fixed in this revision.\n\nThe idea is that we ignore it, then boot to RW. After some time (e.g. after receiving a signal from AP), RW will unlock ROLLBACK region, and on next reboot we can increment it (see comment above, and updated TEST\u003d line).\n\nThis should allow some sort of recovery in case we flash a bad RW with a new rollback version.",
